\n0\n$$\n\nUsing the relationship between multiplication and division, we can write our problem as follows:\n$0$\n\nTo write this fraction as a percentage, we write an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{35}{20} = \\dfrac{35 \\times 5}{20 \\times 5} = \\dfrac{175}{100}\n$$\n\nNow we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{175}{100} = 175 \\%\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147147 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13065" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147147 #edb/ref 1071 "If $0$ then $0$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147147 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "146d6a70-f2ed-5f9a-9d6a-5e4c856acda0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147147 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the relationship between multiplication and division, we can write our problem as follows:\n$0$\n\nWe can simplify this fraction as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{7}{35} = \\dfrac{7 \\div 7}{35 \\div 7} = \\dfrac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nTo write this fraction as a percentage, we write an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{5} = \\dfrac{1 \\times 20}{5 \\times 20} = \\dfrac{20}{100}\n$$\n\nNow we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{20}{100} = 20\\%\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147573 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147573 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147573 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186147862 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147573 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186147876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147573 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding a Missing Percentage Given Two Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147573 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186147146 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147573 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "a2cfba3f-e03a-5cf2-8f7d-9b5576c8eb91" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147574 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049733 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147574 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186147861 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147574 #edb/ref 1038 #