se the relationship between multiplication and division.\n\nTo demonstrate, let's determine the missing number below.\n\n$$\n0\n$$\n\nWe can interpret the word \"of\" as multiplication:\n$0$\n\nNow, using the relationship between multiplication and division, we can write our problem as follows:\n$0$\n\nTo write this fraction as a percentage, we write an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{7}{10} = \\dfrac{7 \\times 10}{10 \\times 10} = \\dfrac{70}{100}\n$$\n\nNow we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{70}{100} = 70\\%\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n70 \\% \\,\\,\\text{of}\\,\\, 10 = 7\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148780 #edb/ref 1065 8169 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148780 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "41806a6e-def6-586b-a059-4450f0974244" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148780 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
